{"instruction": "Implement a function replayupd that filter data based on conditions for a trading system", "input": "", "output": "replayupd:{[f;tabs;syms;t;x]\n  // escape if the table is not one of the subscription tables\n  if[not (t in tabs) or tabs ~ `;:()];\n  // if subscribing for all syms then call upd and then escape\n  if[(syms ~ `)or 99=type syms; f[t;x];:()];\n  // filter down on syms\n  // assuming the the log is storing messages (x) as arrays as opposed to tables\n  c:cols[`. t];\n  // convert x into a table\n  x:select from $[type[x] in 98 99h; x; 0>type first x;enlist c!x;flip c!x] where sym in syms;\n  // call upd on the data\n  f[t;x]\n }"}
{"instruction": "Provide a q function to implement a function replayupd that filter data based on conditions", "input": "", "output": "replayupd:{[f;tabs;syms;t;x]\n  // escape if the table is not one of the subscription tables\n  if[not (t in tabs) or tabs ~ `;:()];\n  // if subscribing for all syms then call upd and then escape\n  if[(syms ~ `)or 99=type syms; f[t;x];:()];\n  // filter down on syms\n  // assuming the the log is storing messages (x) as arrays as opposed to tables\n  c:cols[`. t];\n  // convert x into a table\n  x:select from $[type[x] in 98 99h; x; 0>type first x;enlist c!x;flip c!x] where sym in syms;\n  // call upd on the data\n  f[t;x]\n }"}
{"instruction": "Write q code that implement a function replayupd that filter data based on conditions efficiently", "input": "", "output": "replayupd:{[f;tabs;syms;t;x]\n  // escape if the table is not one of the subscription tables\n  if[not (t in tabs) or tabs ~ `;:()];\n  // if subscribing for all syms then call upd and then escape\n  if[(syms ~ `)or 99=type syms; f[t;x];:()];\n  // filter down on syms\n  // assuming the the log is storing messages (x) as arrays as opposed to tables\n  c:cols[`. t];\n  // convert x into a table\n  x:select from $[type[x] in 98 99h; x; 0>type first x;enlist c!x;flip c!x] where sym in syms;\n  // call upd on the data\n  f[t;x]\n }"}
{"instruction": "In q/kdb+, Implement a function replayupd that filter data based on conditions efficiently in a tick database", "input": "", "output": "replayupd:{[f;tabs;syms;t;x]\n  // escape if the table is not one of the subscription tables\n  if[not (t in tabs) or tabs ~ `;:()];\n  // if subscribing for all syms then call upd and then escape\n  if[(syms ~ `)or 99=type syms; f[t;x];:()];\n  // filter down on syms\n  // assuming the the log is storing messages (x) as arrays as opposed to tables\n  c:cols[`. t];\n  // convert x into a table\n  x:select from $[type[x] in 98 99h; x; 0>type first x;enlist c!x;flip c!x] where sym in syms;\n  // call upd on the data\n  f[t;x]\n }"}
{"instruction": "Provide a q function to implement a function replayupd that filter data based on conditions in a production environment", "input": "", "output": "replayupd:{[f;tabs;syms;t;x]\n  // escape if the table is not one of the subscription tables\n  if[not (t in tabs) or tabs ~ `;:()];\n  // if subscribing for all syms then call upd and then escape\n  if[(syms ~ `)or 99=type syms; f[t;x];:()];\n  // filter down on syms\n  // assuming the the log is storing messages (x) as arrays as opposed to tables\n  c:cols[`. t];\n  // convert x into a table\n  x:select from $[type[x] in 98 99h; x; 0>type first x;enlist c!x;flip c!x] where sym in syms;\n  // call upd on the data\n  f[t;x]\n }"}
{"instruction": "Show me how to implement a function replayupd that filter data based on conditions in a production environment", "input": "", "output": "replayupd:{[f;tabs;syms;t;x]\n  // escape if the table is not one of the subscription tables\n  if[not (t in tabs) or tabs ~ `;:()];\n  // if subscribing for all syms then call upd and then escape\n  if[(syms ~ `)or 99=type syms; f[t;x];:()];\n  // filter down on syms\n  // assuming the the log is storing messages (x) as arrays as opposed to tables\n  c:cols[`. t];\n  // convert x into a table\n  x:select from $[type[x] in 98 99h; x; 0>type first x;enlist c!x;flip c!x] where sym in syms;\n  // call upd on the data\n  f[t;x]\n }"}
